---
title: Year Overview
---

# Year Overview

The Year Overview answers the question "how did my whole year go?". It shows
every day of every year that has data as one calendar, with each day coloured
by a figure that you choose.

## What it shows

### The calendar

Each year has its own calendar. The newest year is at the top. Each square is
one day, and each column is one week. Next to the year, the report shows how
many days have data.

The colour of a square shows the figure that you choose in the menu above the
calendars:

| Figure | What the colour shows |
|--------|-----------------------|
| **Avg Glucose** | The average glucose of the day |
| **Time in Range** | The part of the day from 70 to 180 mg/dL |
| **Bolus** | The bolus insulin of the day |
| **Basal** | The basal insulin of the day |
| **TDD** | The total daily dose of insulin |
| **Carbs** | The carbs of the day |

The colour scale next to the menu shows which colour goes with which value.
For **Avg Glucose**, a day below range or above range also has a hatch pattern.

Move the pointer over a day to see its details: the average glucose, the
insulin (**Bolus**, **Basal** and **TDD**), the **Carbs**, and the number of
records of each type.

### Glycemic Risk Index, month by month

Under each calendar, a chart shows your Glycemic Risk Index (GRI) for each
month. The GRI puts the risk of lows and highs into one score, from 0 to 100. A
lower score means less risk. The chart has five zones:

| Zone | GRI |
|------|-----|
| A | 0-20 |
| B | 21-40 |
| C | 41-60 |
| D | 61-80 |
| E | 81-100 |

Each dot is one month. The horizontal axis is the part of the risk that comes
from lows. The vertical axis is the part that comes from highs. Move the
pointer over a dot to see the score, and the average glucose, insulin and carbs
for that month. The panel next to the chart shows the latest score and its
zone. The chart shows when a year has data for more than one month.

The app shows glucose values in mmol/L if you chose mmol/L.

## How to use it

To change what the colours show:

1. Open the menu above the calendars. It shows **Avg Glucose** first.
2. Select a figure, for example **Time in Range**.
3. Read the colour scale to see which colour means a high value.

To look closer at part of the year:

- Select a day to open it in [Day in Review](/docs/reports/day-in-review).
- Select a week number under the calendar to open that week in
  [Week to Week](/docs/reports/week-to-week).
- Select a month name to open that month in the calendar.

To filter the data:

- Use **All Data Sources** to show the data from some sources only. The
  calendars load again.
- Use **Types** to choose which record types the counts include.

To change the colour scale:

- Move the two handles on the scale, or type a value above each handle, to set
  the range of values that the colours cover. The days outside the range fade.
  Type a value in **Dim outside** to set how much they fade.
- Select **Color boundary** to add a point to the scale. Move the point to
  change where the colours change.
- Select the circle at an end of the scale, or next to a point, to choose a
  different colour for it.
- Select **Swap colors** to put the colours at the two ends in the opposite
  order. For example, to make low values the brightest.
- Select **Reset** to go back to the default scale.

When you scroll down, the scale panel moves out of view. Scroll up a small
distance to show it again at the top of the screen. To make the panel smaller,
select the arrow at its right side. The smaller panel shows only the menu and
the colour scale.

## Good to know

- The report loads one year at a time. Older years load when you scroll down to
  them.
- A day with records but no value for the chosen figure shows in a plain muted
  colour. A day with no records is almost blank.
